  "summary": "A malicious or compromised server can send a reply line that never ends, which",
  "details": "A malicious or compromised server can send a reply line that never ends, which\nthe client buffers until memory runs out. A reply made of many short lines also\nkeeps a CPU core busy: for a few seconds per reply since 0.11.22, for as long\nas the server wants before it.\n\nApplications that connect only to a trusted server over implicit TLS are not\nexposed; the risk applies to clients that may connect to untrusted servers, or\nthat use `STARTTLS` or no TLS, where a man-in-the-middle can forge the reply.",
